course: dictionary
lesson: 935
title: Blink and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. To blink is to shut and open your eyes very quickly. «She did not blink when the loud bang went off» means she showed no fear, while «the warning light began to blink» means it went on and off quickly.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In «in the blink of an eye», blink is part of a phrase, and the whole phrase means very, very quickly. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "very, very quickly" fits, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Blink can also be a noun, so you can have a blink. «Some of the fastest movements are tiny: a trap-jaw ant's jaws close faster than you could ever blink.» Here a blink is the quick shut-and-open of your eyes, and the sentence tells you it is very fast.
fact: To blink means to shut and open your eyes very quickly.
fact: A light can blink, which means it goes on and off quickly.
fact: «In the blink of an eye» means very, very quickly.
fact: «Without blinking» means without showing fear or surprise.
fact: Blinking keeps your eyes wet and clean.
exercise: «The bang was loud, but Sam did not blink.» What does blink mean here? | Shut and opened his eyes very quickly | *Showed no fear or surprise | Shouted back at the noise | Turned round and ran away
exercise: «The warning light began to blink on the dashboard.» What does blink mean here? | Make a loud noise | *Go on and off quickly | Stay bright and still | Fall off the dashboard
exercise: Finish the phrase: «It was over in the ___ of an eye.» | stare | *blink | sneeze | jump
test: Why might people blink less when they stare at a screen? | They are falling asleep | *Their eyes can feel dry | They are reading out loud | Their eyes are getting bigger
test: In «She gave him a quick blink», which word is a noun? | *blink | him | gave | quick
exam: Which sentence uses blink to mean go on and off quickly? | «It was all done in the blink of an eye.» | *«The red light began to blink on and off.» | «He gave a slow blink to show he was tired.» | «She did not blink at the loud bang.»
